@clawsweeper re-review

Both concrete findings are repaired on `ac8fe164333e69a42ad6a7df3f920f82b9a5efb0`. The widget disposes and rebinds a retired session observation, with captured-observation guards against stale reads. Interrupted children now use the existing stopped-outcome classifier. Both final regressions fail against the previously published production source and pass after repair; 94 affected tests, UI types, targeted lint and formatting pass. No CSS or visual presentation changed, so the inspected screenshots remain applicable. The PR body and proof are current.

The area-owner decision about separating authored completion from runtime outcome remains explicitly outstanding; this update does not claim that approval.
